{"schema_version":"obstruction-proposal-v3-shadow-r1","obstruction_id":"O-NS-B1a3b1b-STANDARD-ENSTROPHY-TIME-TRACE","kind":"ENDPOINT_SCALE_CRITICALITY","trigger_signature":["finite time-integrated enstrophy","standard absolute vortex-stretching bound","attempted L-infinity or small one-slice critical enstrophy production"],"statement":"The standard absolute enstrophy closure y'<=C y^3 is compatible with finite-integral scale-critical growth y~(T-t)^(-1/2); therefore it cannot by itself break Type-I scaling or force a small late rescaled-enstrophy slice.","supporting_episode_ids":["EP-NS-B1a3b1b-C001-R1-20260811"],"diagnosis_ids":["DX-NS-B1a3b1b-C001-R1-20260811"],"boundaries":["scalar proof-architecture obstruction only","not an NSE counterexample","local/global gluing not part of the obstruction","stronger equation-specific sign/coherence/frequency information may evade it"],"falsifier_for_obstruction":"Exhibit a theorem derived from exactly the retained scalar hypotheses y>=0, y∈L1, y'<=Cy^3 that forces bounded y or a sequence with sqrt(T-t)y below an arbitrary prescribed positive threshold; the explicit y_a profile blocks such a theorem.","authority":"OBSERVED_ONLY_PROPOSAL_SHADOW","artifact_hash":"sha256:33f9c5f89f544d54499d57b15b6c3e6f85b2bc4987bb4e35ec508200dfaa5653"}
